            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ninad Palsule",
                        "email": "ninad@linux.ibm.com",
                        "username": "ninadpalsule"
                    },
                    "message": "@geissonator@yahoo.com Romulus not supported anymore so should we remove it from CI or we want to fix the issue?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Update: Ninad and I talked today. The main use of Romulus right now is for it's QEMU/CI support up at https://jenkins.openbmc.org/job/CI-MISC/job/run-ci-in-qemu/. If we could get something like p10bmc running in place of that then I'm all for removing romulus. But until then, I think it's required for the project to give us some confidence a openbmc/openbmc commit is good."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ninad Palsule",
                        "email": "ninad@linux.ibm.com",
                        "username": "ninadpalsule"
                    },
                    "message": "FYI... I just talked to Joel and he suggested to continue with Romulus CI as that is the only boot test for ast2500. Jeol and AndrewJ are looking at the image size issue."
                }
            ],
